-- title:
--   Existence and uniqueness of the value homomorphism at a place
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $F$ be a field extension of $K$. Fix a valuation subring $A$ of $K$, an element $g \in F$, and a subring $B_0$ of $F$. Write $C$ for the subring of $F$ generated by the image of $A$ under $K \to F$ together with $g$, i.e. `Subring.closure (algebraMap K F '' (A : Set K) ∪ {g})`. The hypothesis `hint` requires that every $b \in B_0$ be integral over $C$: there is a monic polynomial $p$ with coefficients in $C$ whose evaluation at $b$, after mapping the coefficients into $F$, vanishes. Let $w$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_w$ of $F$ which contains $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F(a)$ for every $a \in K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring; assume further that $g$ is congruent to a constant from $A$ at $w$, namely that $g - \mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F(a)$ lies in the nonunits of $\mathcal{O}_w$ for some $a \in A$. Then there is exactly one ring homomorphism $\varphi : B_0 \to A$ such that for all $b \in B_0$ the difference $b - \mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,F(\varphi(b))$ is a nonunit of $\mathcal{O}_w$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between places and residue values: membership of $b - c$ in the nonunits of $\mathcal{O}_w$ says that $b$ is congruent to the constant $c$ modulo the maximal ideal at $w$, so the statement produces the reduction map $B_0 \to A$ attached to $w$ and shows it is the only such map. It is used in the theory of characteristic-$p$ models of modular curves, in particular by [`ModularCurve.valuation_lt_one_of_sub_mem_nonunits_of_coeff_lt_one_inf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.valuation_lt_one_of_sub_mem_nonunits_of_coeff_lt_one_inf).
